wikipedia_extract: 'USS Ranger (CV-4) was an interwar United States Navy aircraft
  carrier, the only ship of its class.  A Treaty ship, Ranger was the first U.S. vessel
  to be designed and built from the keel up as a carrier.  She was relatively small,
  just 730 ft (220 m) long and under 15,000 tons, closer in size and displacement
  to the first US carrier—Langley—than later ships. An island superstructure was not
  included in the original design, but was added after completion.

  Deemed too slow for use with the Pacific Fleet''s carrier task forces against Japan,
  she spent most of World War II in the Atlantic Ocean, where the German fleet, the
  Kriegsmarine, was a weaker opponent. Ranger saw combat in that theater and provided
  air support for Operation Torch. In October 1943, she fought in Operation Leader,
  air attacks on German shipping off Norway. She was sold for scrap in 1947.'
